  "hints": [
    "Make every rule the same shape: a function that takes the fee so far and the minutes and returns a new fee. What does the engine then have to do to price a stay?",
    "Keep the rules in an ordered list and fold over it in fee(). A map from rule name to a factory (params in, rule out) lets addRule reject unknown names and means a new rule type is one new entry.",
    "fee(minutes) = apply each rule in order, starting from ceil(minutes / 60) * rate. The cap multiplies by ceil(minutes / 1440), the discount is floor(fee * (100 - percent) / 100), and minimum leaves a fee of 0 alone."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(R) per fee() call for R rules; addRule and removeRule are O(R)",
    "space": "O(R)"
  }
}
